# GKE COS kubelet vs in-cluster HTTP registry (ADR-010)
# Repro: TARGET=gke, Cap/addon image = http://<ClusterIP>:5000/...
# kubelet speaks HTTPS to registries by default.
#
# Typical node event (ImagePullBackOff):
#   Failed to pull image: http: server gave HTTP response to HTTPS client
#
# configure-gke-registry-pull.sh writes containerd hosts.toml; on COS it often
# does not stick without a node recycle. We did not use that as the install path.
#
# Workaround: docker.io/muralisvishnu/halden-cage:* over HTTPS + Secret dockerhub-creds.
# Kind remains the private-registry + air-gap proof.
#
# Code: environment/scripts/configure-gke-registry-pull.sh
#       scripts/install.sh TARGET=gke HELM_EXTRA Hub --sets
